request.description:
The last 30 days for the signed `(app, tenant)`, grouped by the app's own model alias (plan.md §6, §13).

**Auth:** per-app HMAC — layer 1 of §12.1. GET has no body, so the canonical string hashes the empty string; the TARGET it signs includes the query string.

**200 response:**
```json
{
  "from": "2026-06-30", "to": "2026-07-29",
  "groupBy": "model",
  "groups": [
    { "key": "balanced", "unit": "input_tokens",
      "qty": 1200, "costUsdEstimate": "0.003600000000" }
  ],
  "days":   [
    { "day": "2026-07-29", "unit": "input_tokens",
      "qty": 1200, "costUsdEstimate": "0.003600000000" }
  ]
}
```

`groups` totals the window at the requested grain; `days` is the aggregate's own grain, so a caller can chart or reconcile one day. §13's "expose both".

`key` is null when nothing attributed the usage — what a CLI catalog probe looks like.

**Problem types:** `400 invalid_input` (a window that is not two real UTC days, backwards, or over 400 days), `401 unauthorized`, `403 app_suspended`, `429 rate_limited`, `503 store_unavailable`.

